{
  "title": "Coupling-modulated ring, PAM4 (MZI coupler)",
  "group": "Lasers & modulators",
  "description": "53.125 GBd PAM4 on a coupling-modulated silicon microring built from parts: two 50/50 directional couplers and series push-pull PN-junction phase shifters form an MZI coupler. The design point (arm phase bias, laser detuning, 1.65-3.65 V drive) keeps the swing on the under-coupled flank for evenly spaced levels: RLM 0.98, ER 4.0 dB, OMA 0.46 mW, IL 1.2 dB, tolerant to +-0.5 pm of drift. Quasi-static optics (steady-state waveguides): the eye shows level placement, not photon-lifetime bandwidth",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -340,
        "title": "Coupling-modulated ring, PAM4 \u2014 what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "A microring whose bus coupler is itself an MZI: 50/50",
          "couplers DC1/DC2 bound two arms, each a 400 um depletion",
          "PN phase shifter (PN_A bus side, PN_B ring side); WG_R1 +",
          "WG_R2 close the ring. Series push-pull: PRBS drives the",
          "middle node, so PN_A sees V_R = v and PN_B 4 V - v. The arm",
          "phase difference sets k_eff^2 = cos^2(dphi/2) while the",
          "ring's round-trip phase (its resonance) stays put.",
          "PAM4 design point: 53.125 GBd PRBS13 PAM4, 1.65..3.65 V",
          "(2 Vpp). WG_A is 240 nm longer than WG_B, which puts the",
          "whole swing on the under-coupled flank (notch -6.4 dB ->",
          "-1.3 dB), and LAS sits 2-3 pm blue of resonance, where the",
          "levels come out evenly spaced: RLM 0.98, ER 4.0 dB, OMA",
          "0.46 mW, IL 1.2 dB. Eye and Link tabs: levels, BER, TDECQ.",
          "The catch is Q ~ 50k: RLM holds >= 0.95 only within",
          "+-0.5 pm of laser-resonance drift. Steady-state waveguides",
          "make the optics quasi-static: the eye shows level placement,",
          "not photon-lifetime bandwidth.",
          "",
          "Vary * (all) wavelength_nm = 1310.012, 1310.014, 1310.016",
          "and re-run: 2 pm of drift bunches the ladder (RLM ~0.84)."
        ]
      }
    ],
